  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(CVIM) Accelerating development of novel vaccines via support to the UK Centre for Veterinary Vaccine Innovation &amp; Manufacturing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Centre for Veterinary Vaccine Innovation &amp; Manufacturing (CVIM) has been set up to bridge a gap between basic research and late-stage product development of vaccines. New technology (for example RNA vaccines) has the potential to transform vaccine development, but currently low-cost livestock vaccines utilising emerging technology are not being developed for deployment in developing countries. The overall objective of the centre is to accelerate the development and production of vaccines for the most challenging, and urgent livestock diseases, including those that can spread to humans (zoonotic diseases) and cause significant productivity loss in Low- and Middle-income Countries (LMICs). 
By accelerating the development of novel vaccines for high consequence livestock diseases with commercial partners in both developed and developing countries, the programme will improve vaccine access and use and consequently improve the livelihoods of livestock farmers and economic wellbeing and food security in LIDCs. It will enable international trade and protect human health. 
The programme will build on existing capability at the Pirbright Institute, UK, leveraging Pirbright&#x2019;s high containment facilities for laboratory and animal studies and expertise in veterinary virology, immunology, and vaccine development.</narrative>
  </description>
